{"nodes": [{"id": "client_release_remediation_report_document", "label": "FreshFlow Client Release Remediation Report", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "CLIENT_RELEASE_REMEDIATION_REPORT.md", "source_location": "L1", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "client_release_remediation_report_conditional_release_decision", "label": "Conditional release decision", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLIENT_RELEASE_REMEDIATION_REPORT.md", "source_location": "L14", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "**Release decision:** **CONDITIONAL NO-GO \u2014 the repaired application passes its code and browser test gates, but the external security, production-data, Git, deployment, recovery, and client-acceptance gates below are still mandatory** ## 0. Remediation execution update \u2014 18 September 2026"}, {"id": "client_release_remediation_report_httponly_cookie_authentication", "label": "HttpOnly cookie authentication", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLIENT_RELEASE_REMEDIATION_REPORT.md", "source_location": "L60", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "- Added cookie and bearer authentication with `/auth/me` and `/auth/logout`; cookies are HttpOnly, SameSite, environment-aware, and API authorization still validates the signed token and active user. - Added router authentication to master data, SKU mappings, procurement, packing, invoicing, operations, and protected order reads; added role gates to commercial mutations. - Added audit records for SKU mapping and selling-price changes. - Enforced 25 MB workbook limits, `.xlsx`/`.xlsm` types, sanitized temporary filenames, chunked writes, cleanup, and controlled 4xx responses."}, {"id": "client_release_remediation_report_signed_handoff_integrity", "label": "Signed handoff integrity", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLIENT_RELEASE_REMEDIATION_REPORT.md", "source_location": "L67", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "- Corrected Handoff 01 zero-quantity handling and made both handoff payloads hash exactly the immutable JSON that is persisted. - Added packing weight capture with net/gross, item-total, capacity, stage, lock, and role validation. - Added same-order/route/date, material, capacity, and lock safeguards to box transfers and invalidated stale weights after a material transfer. - Added final-pack locking for authorized managers/system administrators and Handoff 02 return."}, {"id": "client_release_remediation_report_canonical_commercial_data_approval", "label": "Canonical commercial data approval", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLIENT_RELEASE_REMEDIATION_REPORT.md", "source_location": "L169", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "#### Gate C \u2014 Canonical production data 1. Have the catalogue owner decide every R-007 collision and every unresolved September row. 2. Import approved main/sub-customer legal names, billing addresses/emails, destinations, and tax/VAT identifiers."}, {"id": "client_release_remediation_report_production_deployment_gate", "label": "Production deployment gate", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLIENT_RELEASE_REMEDIATION_REPORT.md", "source_location": "L179", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "#### Gate D \u2014 Production deployment 1. Configure HTTPS `PUBLIC_APP_URL`, production `CORS_ORIGINS`, Supabase pooler URL, strong `SECRET_KEY`, Redis, and one-time seed password through secrets/configuration. 2. Build both Docker images from the recovered release commit on a host with a working daemon."}, {"id": "client_release_remediation_report_recovery_and_acceptance_gate", "label": "Recovery and acceptance gate", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLIENT_RELEASE_REMEDIATION_REPORT.md", "source_location": "L189", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "#### Gate E \u2014 Operations, recovery, and acceptance 1. Configure structured logs, error alerting, uptime/readiness monitoring, and security-event review. 2. Define database/file backup frequency, retention, encryption, owners, RPO, and RTO; complete a restore drill."}, {"id": "client_release_remediation_report_historical_payment_and_receipt_workflow", "label": "Historical payment and receipt workflow", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLIENT_RELEASE_REMEDIATION_REPORT.md", "source_location": "L22", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The application is no longer blocked by the original integrated workflow defects. Authentication, order intake, procurement, both signed handoffs, packing weights and locks, invoicing, payment control, receipts, reconciliation, and live dashboards now have working code paths and automated coverage. A live browser walkthrough also loaded the seeded operational data in every main workstation. The repository must **not** yet be represented as production-ready or delivered as a final client release. The remaining blockers cannot be safely invented or completed from source code alone: the corrupt Git repository must be recovered, canonical product"}, {"id": "client_release_remediation_report_current_production_baseline", "label": "Current production baseline", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "CLIENT_RELEASE_REMEDIATION_REPORT.md", "source_location": "L3", "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "> **Historical report notice \u2014 reconciled 26 October 2026:** prior fixes, release > decisions and test counts below remain historical evidence. The > [production baseline](docs/audits/2026-10-26/PRODUCTION_BASELINE.md), > [current audit](docs/audits/2026-10-26/REPORT.md) and"}], "edges": [{"source": "c